# Feature: SKU Creation and Management

## Short Description

SKU (Stock Keeping Unit) Creation and Management is a feature used to give each inventory item a unique identification code. The SKU helps the store identify, organize, and track individual products efficiently.

## Purpose

The purpose of SKU management is to provide a consistent and unique way of identifying products in a store. It makes it easier to locate items, monitor stock levels, record transactions, and distinguish between products that may have similar names or descriptions.

## Main Functions/Activities

- Create unique SKU codes for new products.
- Assign SKUs based on product characteristics such as product type, brand, size, color, or model.
- Store important product information such as product name, description, category, and unit of measurement.
- Edit or update product information when necessary.
- Search for products using their SKU or other identifying information.
- Prevent duplicate SKU codes.
- Deactivate or archive SKUs for discontinued products.
- Link SKUs to stock quantities and inventory transactions.
- Organize products into categories for easier management.
